{"act": 23, "action": "documents.compose", "actor": "e2e", "at": "2026-11-21T17:40:07+00:00", "input": {"body": "# Closure review \u2014 S01 UI spike\n\n## Outcome vs acceptance\n\nThe declared gate is \"the decision record states what is observable and marks the rest not\nrecoverable.\" The ADR records CSR as the decision with the measured TTI, first render, bundle, drag,\nauth and cold-build numbers, and names the values that were never measured.\n\n## Evidence\n\nADR 0001 (`docs/decisions/0001-ui-stack.md`), the acceptance manifest, and the slice plan. The\nobservable numbers are the ADR's measured table; the spike workspace (`spikes/web`) was deleted after\nthe ADR, so the raw runs are gone.\n\n## Open items\n\nMetrics 5\u20137 are **not recoverable**: metric 5 was captured once for CSR and never for SSR; metric 6 was\nskipped by the time-box; metric 7's SSR set is two runs, stated not averaged. Re-running the spike\nwould be a new project and is not claimed here.\n\n## Decision\n\nClose the project. The original closure row (2026-11-17) remains; this review supersedes it and is\ndated 2026-11-21.\n", "category": "closure-review", "project_id": "01a1d039-0d27-724c-9bae-af96b2d926b1", "publishable": true, "title": "Closure review \u2014 S01 (retrospective, 2026-11-21)"}, "result_id": "01a1ff31-9ce6-76cb-8bfc-1812a99646e3"}
